  "worked_solution": "In this context, the area $A$ under the curve $y=r(t)$ over the interval $[0,60]$ represents the number of corn kernels popped by the machine in one minute\n\nThe general formula for the trapezoidal rule states that\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[r(a)+2(r({t}_{1})+r({t}_{2})+⋯+r({t}_{n-1}))+r(b)]Δt,\n$$\n\nwhere $n$ is the number of trapezoids and $Δt=\\frac{b-a}{n}$ is the step size.\n\nHere, we have the following values:\n\n- The number of trapezoids is $n=3.$\n\n- The corresponding interval is $[0,60],$ so we have $a=0$ and $b=60.$\n\n- The step size is given by\n\n$$\nΔt=\\frac{b-a}{n}=\\frac{60-0}{3}=20.\n$$\n\nUsing the above values, the general formula becomes\n\n$$\nA≈\\frac{1}{2}[r(0)+2(r(20)+r(40))+r(60)]\\cdot 20.\n$$\n\nSubstituting the appropriate numbers from the given table in the above expression gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & ≈\\frac{1}{2}[40+2(50+50)+30]\\cdot 20 \\\\  & =10(270) \\\\  & =2\\,700.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the machine pops approximately $2\\,700$ in the given one-minute period.",
